      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Mankato"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Railroads arrived in 1868, turning Mankato into southern Minnesota’s railroad hub and ending the era of steamboat travel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
